<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia to buy 33 trains from Siemens, Fiat.</title>
<headline>Slovenia to buy 33 trains from Siemens, Fiat.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenia's government said on Thursday it decided to buy 33 new trains worth 180 million German marks ($97.6 million) from Siemens and Fiat for the state-owned Slovenian railway.</p>
<p>&quot;We chose Siemens because their joint offer with Fiat was the best,&quot; the Minister of Traffic Anton Bergauer told a news conference.</p>
<p>He said the contract with Siemens was expected to be signed later this year while the trains should be delivered over the next five years.</p>
<p>Among the bidders were Adtranz, Moravskoslezka Vagonka, Breda, GEC Alsthom and DWA.</p>
<p>-- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
